      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually it still has the bitmask meaning: please take a look at these twos about the use case as bit-mask.\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/tpm2/+/1892419.\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/third_party/tpm2/+/1893681\n\nThe existing TPM vendor command header of ours has a header like:\n    | Tag(2B) | Length (4B) | Command (4B, 0x2000 0000) | sub-command (2B) | body |\n\nIn Fido Command supporting patches, I add another case, which is named \u0027TPM extended command\u0027.\nThe header is like:\n    | Tag(2B) | Length (4B) | Command (4B, 0x2000 XXXX) | body |\n                                                  ^^^^\n                                                  (TPM Command Code in 2B)",
